# Frontend Layered Architecture

Three layers, each with a single responsibility. Dependencies point one way only.

```
view -> store -> service -> api
```

## Layer 1 - view (`src/view`)

- Components and pages own rendering and user interaction.
- May use `useAppSelector`, `useAppDispatch`, and local `useState`.
- Do not import from `service/` or call endpoints directly.
- May import error classes from `api/errors` for `instanceof` checks.
- Presentational components take props only; connected components select/dispatch and compose them.

## Layer 2 - service (`src/service`)

- One exported function per use case.
- Owns orchestration, mapping response -> domain model, and business rules.
- Pure helpers live in `mappers/` and `rules/`.
- Never imports axios or the store.
- Lets api errors propagate unless a business rule needs a fallback.

## Layer 2 - store (`src/store`)

- `createAsyncThunk` calls exactly one service function and `rejectWithValue(error)`.
- Rejected case stores the error as-is: `state.error = action.payload`.
- Components decide what to do with `instanceof` on that error.
- `serializableCheck` is disabled so `Error` instances can live in state.

## Layer 3 - api (`src/api`)

- Only this layer talks to the network (axios `client`).
- Each endpoint wraps its call in try/catch and throws via `mapAxiosError` (or the same mapping inline).
- Response body types live in `api/responses/` (one type per endpoint success shape).
- Error mapping:
  - no response -> `ConnectionError`
  - `401` -> `UnauthorizedError`
  - `422` -> `ValidationError` (fields from array of single-key objects)
  - any other status -> `UnexpectedError`
- Never imports the store or a component.

## Naming conventions

- Endpoint module: `{resource}Endpoints.ts`
- Service: `{area}Service.ts`
- Mapper: `{resource}Mapper.ts`
- Slice: `{resource}Slice.ts`, thunk names `'{resource}/{action}'`
- Domain model in `types/`; response type in `api/responses/` suffixed (`ResourceResponse`)
